Session A:
T1: read Bob balance = 100, application calculates 100 - 10 = 90
+----+------------+---------+
| id | owner_name | balance |
+----+------------+---------+
|  2 | Bob        |     100 |
+----+------------+---------+

Session B:
T2: also reads Bob balance = 100, application calculates 100 - 30 = 70
+----+------------+---------+
| id | owner_name | balance |
+----+------------+---------+
|  2 | Bob        |     100 |
+----+------------+---------+

Session B:
T2: committed Bob balance = 70
+----+------------+---------+
| id | owner_name | balance |
+----+------------+---------+
|  2 | Bob        |      70 |
+----+------------+---------+

Session A:
T1: final value is 90, so T2 update to 70 was lost
+----+------------+---------+
| id | owner_name | balance |
+----+------------+---------+
|  2 | Bob        |      90 |
+----+------------+---------+

Result: final balance is 90 instead of expected 60, because Session A overwrote Session B.
